# Instant Pot Beef Stew

Originally adapted from [The Kitchn](https://www.thekitchn.com/instant-pot-beef-stew-22949287) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251021094246/https://www.thekitchn.com/instant-pot-beef-stew-22949287))

{ rating="4" image="instant_pot_beef_stew.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Stew

- [ ] 1 lb [boneless beef chuck]{ ing="boneless-beef-chuck" }, cut into 1.5” pieces
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, plus more as needed
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, plus more as needed
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } or vegetable oil
- [ ] 1 medium [yellow onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, diced
- [ ] 4 [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, cut into chunks
- [ ] 2 [celery stalks]{ ing="celery-stalks" } or green bell pepper, sliced
- [ ] 1 cup [mushrooms]{ ing="mushrooms" }, quartered (optional)
- [ ] 2 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [tomato paste]{ ing="tomato-paste" }
- [ ] 3 cups [vegetable or beef broth]{ ing="vegetable-or-beef-broth" }
- [ ] 3 medium [Yukon Gold potatoes]{ ing="yukon-gold-potatoes" }, cut into 1” cubes
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [Worcestershire sauce]{ ing="worcestershire-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }

### Add Last

- [ ] 1 Tbsp [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 1 cup [frozen peas]{ ing="frozen-peas" }
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [dried Fine Herbs]{ ing="dried-fine-herbs" } (or Parsley)

## Recipe

1. Season beef with [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }. Set Instant Pot to Sauté (High). Working in batches, brown beef in [oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } on all sides. Remove and set aside
1. Add [onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, celery, and [mushrooms]{ ing="mushrooms" } to pot. Cook ~5 minutes until softened
1. Add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } and [tomato paste]{ ing="tomato-paste" } and cook 1 minute
1. Add [broth]{ ing="vegetable-or-beef-broth" } and scrape bottom to release browned bits
1. Return beef to pot. Add remaining broth, [potatoes]{ ing="yukon-gold-potatoes" }, [thyme]{ ing="dried-thyme" }, [Worcestershire sauce]{ ing="worcestershire-sauce" }, and [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }. Lock lid
1. Cook on HIGH pressure for 25 minutes. Natural release 10 minutes, then quick release
1. Whisk [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" } and [water]{ ing="water" } together, then stir into stew along with [frozen peas]{ ing="frozen-peas" } and [Fine Herbs]{ ing="dried-fine-herbs" }. Cook on Saute for 2 minutes until thickened

## Notes

- Can use leaner beef (top sirloin or round) for healthier version
- Tastes better day 2-3 and freezes well
